    {
      "id": "_jfmzfGmyjkIVoIfdQKaz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 415.2904051816406,
      "y": 617.201294,
      "width": 668.8795776367188,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aY",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 265850769,
      "version": 653,
      "versionNonce": 2024095697,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791206337868,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Every thread runs the SAME code.\nThe only thing that differs is the numbers the GPU Gives it:\nits block and its position in the block.\nBut our data is one flat row, so the GPU's numbers don't say which\nelement is a thread's own.\nIndexing turns them into one number that does.\n\nThis guarantees:\n- every element gets a thread (no gaps)\n- no two threads get the same element (no collisions)\n\nIn the code:\nindex_1d() -> ThreadIndex (used by get_mut to write c)\n.get() -> usize (used to read a[i], b[i]",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Every thread runs the SAME code.\nThe only thing that differs is the numbers the GPU Gives it:\nits block and its position in the block.\nBut our data is one flat row, so the GPU's numbers don't say which\nelement is a thread's own.\nIndexing turns them into one number that does.\n\nThis guarantees:\n- every element gets a thread (no gaps)\n- no two threads get the same element (no collisions)\n\nIn the code:\nindex_1d() -> ThreadIndex (used by get_mut to write c)\n.get() -> usize (used to read a[i], b[i]",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
